  "supersedes": "The earlier frozen config (a=2, r=10, commit 75005575) was superseded: its baseline subtracted the full-record free weekly fit, which removed the weekly noise correlated with the PV shape, and it scored paired differences of two fits sharing one noise draw. This config subtracts the season-year constant fit and scores the fit of baseline plus injection against the known path.",
  "constant_path_redefinition": "The constant-path unit was redefined after the first attempt's tuning results were seen. The first attempt injected a constant capacity from a farm into the semi-synthetic baseline, whose real series still held intra-year growth, so real rises counted as false steps. The constant-path unit now uses the placebo sky: the PV shape is permuted within each month and the known constant capacity times the permuted shape is added back, so the baseline holds no real growth. The change was made on tuning units only. The scoring units were never fitted or touched. The write-up must report both attempts. The limits and the tie rule are unchanged.",
